~
@300  = ~Epée à 2 mains +4: Backbiter~
@301  = ~The Épée à deux mains is a derivative of the Epée longue. Weapon smiths have always looked for ways to improve existing weapons. In an effort to improve the Epée longue, the blade was lengthened. Eventually, the handle had to be extended and two hands became necessary to properly swing the sword. The primary function of Épée à deux mainss is cleaving mounted knights and breaking up pike formations. This one is particularly good at its job as it has been enchanted with a few magique properties.

PARAMETRES:

Dégâts: 1D10 +4 (+1D6 perforant)
